# NOTE: in .gitattributes the LAST matching pattern wins, so the general rule
# must come first and the specific overrides after it.

# Default: let git normalise text in the repository as usual.
* text=auto

# Dataset files must round-trip byte-for-byte on every platform.
#
# The Boiler CSV as distributed by IEEE DataPort uses CRLF line endings, and
# dataset/CHECKSUMS.sha256 records the SHA-256 of exactly those bytes. Under
# git's default text handling (core.autocrlf), the blob would be normalised to
# LF on commit and restored to CRLF only on Windows checkouts - so a reviewer
# on Linux or macOS would get different bytes and a spurious checksum failure.
# Marking these paths binary (-text) disables all end-of-line conversion.
dataset/** -text
